.TH TWEEN 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
Tween \- Animates one float from its current value to a target over a duration with an easing curve, by writing through a pointer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqtween.h\(dq
.ft B
typedef struct Tween {
  float *target;
  float  from, to, duration, elapsed;
  EaseFn ease;
  bool   active;
} Tween;
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Animates one float from its current value to a target over a duration with an easing curve, by writing through a pointer. Presentation state: keep tweens in scene statics and point them at scene statics (a panel's x, a fade alpha, a zoom) or at GameState floats that are purely visual. Start with tween_start(), advance with tween_update() once per update; tween_done() reports completion. One Tween animates one float; a Vec2 needs two.
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.B target
the float being animated; must outlive the tween
.TP
.B from
value when the tween started
.TP
.B to
destination
.TP
.B duration
seconds
.TP
.B elapsed
seconds so far
.TP
.B ease
curve applied to elapsed/duration
.TP
.B active
true until elapsed reaches duration
.SH MODULE
tween (src/engine/tween/tween.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tween_start (3),
.BR tween_update (3),
.BR tween_done (3),
.BR EaseFn (3),
